# The build context for deploy/Containerfile, which is the workspace root.
#
# `COPY . .` is the whole context, so what is listed here is the difference
# between a few megabytes of source and several gigabytes of host build output —
# and, for target/, between a clean build and one whose cache mount is shadowed
# by artefacts cargo built for another platform.

# Host build output. The container builds its own, on a cache mount.
target/

# Worktrees `bd worktree` creates inside the repository. Each is a second copy of
# the whole workspace; one left behind would be copied into the image context and
# built nothing.
gc-*/

# The issue ledger and its lock. Not needed to compile anything, and a database
# file in a build context is a database file in a layer.
.beads/
.beads.gate.lock
*.gate.lock
.dolt/

.git/
.github/
.forgejo/

# Agent instructions and editor settings: text about the code, not the code.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/

# The manifests and the image definition itself. The build needs the workspace,
# not the deployment of it — and deploy/ changes far more often than the source,
# so leaving it in would invalidate the build cache for nothing.
deploy/

# Generated by the release pipeline, never an input to the build.
sbom.spdx.json
